> me) are still too lazy to go and just spend a day or two getting it to
> build properly ...

There is an additional problem that Netscape never was 64 bit clean.  When
they compiled their version for Digital Unix, they supplied a compiler flag
that told it to use 31 bits (to avoid sign extension problems) for pointers.
That allowed them to use crappy code where pointers were assigned to ints and
vice versa.  That crappy code is mostly still there in Mozilla.

