Keith Baker wrote:
> 
> This is what I was trying to do...  Only problem is...  as soon as I start
> xdm it launches x windows on the local machine (local begin the machine
> running xdm

Have a look in the XDM config files which I think are in /usr/X11/lib/X11/xdm
and I think you'll find one called Xservers.  I'm guessing that at the moment
it has a line in which says something like 'local'; I can't remember the
format exactly.  But what you want to do is edit the file so that it doesn't
start one on local (i.e. the local machine running xdm) and make it so that
it will allow connections from other machines.  I think this is what you need
to edit.

Dave
