On May 31, Robert Williams wrote:

> Keith Baker wrote:
> 
> > I'm trying to run a client on one of my machines and use the other as an
> > xterm...  problem is when I start xdm it launches all of x...  including a
> > local xserver...  this is not what I want...  I didn't think xdm needed
> > this...
> 
> Let's call the "client" machine machine.to.connect.to
> and the the "xterm" machine (I assume you really mean
> X Terminal) the X display server, or machine.to.connect.from.
> 
> 1.  Run xdm on  machine.to.connect.to.
> 2.  Don't run xdm (or startx, or any other x wrapper)
>      on machine.to.connect.from.   Instead,  from the ascii
>      console, run    "X -query machine.to.connect.to".
>      This should give you an X loggin display on connect.from
>       for connect.to.

one addition, if you have multiple `machine.to.connect.to's which you'd like
to be able to connect to directly:

start  `X -indirect some.server.host'  (e.g. in inittab) which will give you
a chooser menu first where you can select the host to connect to.


