Hello Jay,

 I noticed `read dev: block' didn't work properly: it just hangs doing
nothing.  Apparently this is caused by a NULL pointer.  I've fixed that
problem, and meanwhile extended the function of read somewhat.  (Instead of
just showing 256 bytes it shows what's on the disk one screenful at a time.)
 Since it's also nice to have an indication as to why milo crashes I also
added `wrent (entMM, 2)' somewhere.  But perhaps that should be called even
earlier.  Now milo will reboot if a memory fault occurs after having
displayed an explanation message.
 Another few lines fixed a few `unresolved symbols' when linking to the free
x86 emulation library.  Though the free library won't work anyway on my
machine.  *Sigh*
 Oh yes, this is against milo-2.0.30-0.4 I think.

					Arnaud

-- 
Arnaud Installe                                 arnaud.installe@advalvas.be 

3rd Law of Computing:
	Anything that can go wr
fortune: Segmentation violation -- Core dumped

