Sorry, but ouups [again]. ;-]

Even good old SunOS can't automatically allocate the struct.
(ok, it theoretically can, but if you call stat(file, NULL); there
is no way to get the allocated "struct stat" pointer back !)
Trust me, it only works if you have a cool random pointer, this is simply
a platform-independent bug that gernerates platform/compiler-dependent 
results... Be careful.

