This is a standard laptop IDE interface (44 pin, includes power and
drive select, IIRC), you probably really do not want to do this, for
the following reasons:

	1) Extremely in-elegant to have cables oozing out of your 
	   system case.

	2) IDE on Multia is DARN SLOW.

	3) It will take power away from your Multia PS, generating
	   more heat.

	4) You will probably have problems as your IDE cable starts
	   to grow much beyond 18".

	5) Are you really that short on space...

These are really very subjective objections, but I think you should
reconsider this approach.  If yo insist on doing this, I suspect that
Mr. Hilarius at Harddata in Canada could make you a cable...

Did I say I didn't think this was a good idea? Just checking...

Good luck,

Ken
khansen@njcc.com

