The Abort problem was reported to egcs-bugs (and CC'd to you) about
3 weeks ago together with a stack trace at the offending function.
If I fail to report anything you need to debug it in a bug report,
you have only to ask and I'll forward the information,

As for the performance, well I keep three performance figures everytime
I build EGCS:
  1) Dhrystone - meaningless but small.
  2) Mesa-2.5, 'trispd' - triangle plotting speed; a good mix of integer
               and floating point.
  3) Povray - Time to render two of the examples; floating point heavy at
              a guess.

The reason I haven't reported the X problem to the EGCS list is that I'm
not sure whether its an X problem or an EGCS problem; and I don't know
enough about the internals of X/VGA text modes/The Matrox millenium etc to
debug it.

