Hi Peter !
 
> I'm using Linux 2.0.33, RedHat 5.0, on two alpha boxes (recently acquired,
> partly on my advice).  GNU Emacs 20.2 hangs quite often and I have to kill
> it to continue (it won't respond to C-g).
> 
> Is this a known problem?  Should I try recompiling Emacs from scratch?
> Any advice?  Any help appreciated!

I think it's caused by the select(...) bug.
Recompile doesn't help because "/usr/include/gnu/types.h" has a
broken __FDMASK definition.
Update glibc (glibc-devel) or change 
/usr/include/gnu/types.h
from
#define __FDMASK(d)     (1 << ((d) % __NFDBITS))
to 
#define __FDMASK(d)     (1UL << ((d) % __NFDBITS))

and then recompile.

