stack setup and unwinding is done inside the kernel.

on a sig, the current environment is placed on the user stack, and the
parameters to the sig handler is placed in registers( the first 6 parms to a
routine are place in registers )
although u should only get a signum as a parameter to the sig handler, i beleive
that there are 2 more. I think the third parameter is a pointer to the saved
area ( as saved by the kern).

unwinding is done when ur sig handler does a jsr 0(26) which then executes a
small pgm left on the stack by the kernel, which then traps to the kern, wher
the kern will fix up the stack and continue from the saved pc address ( while in
the sig routine, u can change the return address to be something else )

