Hello,
I don't know whether this is really going to help. 
I had a similar problem, but with the help of the wonderful linux
enthusiasts out there , I have 7 alphas running RHL 5.0 ( I don't have RHL
5.1) now. My machines are AS200 4/166 with 32M memory and 1 GB SCSI disk.
This is what I did :-

SRM Console:

My SCSI CDROM is scd0 /sr0 ( dka500 ) and HDD is dka0.
I opened and attached a FDD ( dva0) .
Two floppy disks : images/avanti-s.img and images/ramdisk.img were
prepared. ( I used dd in an already running Linux). Rawrite.exe could also
be used from DOS .
I inserted the ramdisk floppy and executed 
boot dka500 -fi kernels/avanti-s.gz -fl "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1"
Alternately , insert the first floppy (avanti-s.img)  and give the
command boot dva0  -fl "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1"
Change the floppy afterwards when prompted.

I got the familiar install screen.
Do the initial install processes. When it comes to partitioning, choose
fdisk . Choose the bsd style disk labelling (b) . Edit the parameters
properly and then start creating the partitions.
a : 2MB : boot
b: adequate : swap
c,d,e .... : adequate : ext2
(w)rite  and then (q)uit.
 It goes thru the swap creation , formatting , package selection ,
installation and finally the configuration. PCI devices are normally
autodetected.

Finally a reboot occurs. This time ,
boot dka500 -fi kernels/avanti-s.gz -fl "root=/dev/sda3" 
						     ^^ choose whatever is
adequate. 
Please make sure that aboot is installed. You will find /sbin/swriteboot
and /boot/bootlx.
Execute the command "swriteboot -f1 -v /dev/sda /boot/bootlx" . It should
write the bootstrap loader. Please lookout for any error messages.
If all's well,
Shutdown and set the appropriate variables ( auto_action , bootdef_dev ,
boot_file , boot_osflags to BOOT, dka0.0.0.6.0, 3/vmlinux.gz and
"root=/dev/sda3" etc.) . sda is the first SCSI disk and partition num 3 is
the root partition for my machines.
Now the system should autoboot to RHL.
Please note that this is the case with RHL 5.0 . I haven't tried RHL5.1	

WInNT ARC Console:
First  a new configuration has to be chosen.
Use From CDROM 
and \milo\arc\linload.exe as loader and \milo\avanti as the file.
You can boot into MILO from the CDROM.
Now create a floppy with /images/avanti.img ( Not avanti-s.img) and insert
it into FDD.
boot fd0 root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1 should start the
installation in a similar way. 
This time Diskdruid/fdisk ay be used and choose the traditional DOS style
partitioning. Keep a 2MB DOS partition for the MILO where
/milo/images/avanti.img can be dumped later.
Installation is similar.
Finally ARC can be configured to boot into MILO from this DOS partition.
If you set the OSLOADOPTIONS as "boot sda3 root=/dev/sda3" or whatever ,
the machine will boot into MILO and then to Linux.

Hope this will at least be of some use.

Regards,
-Mohanan P G



