The file in question, which "officially" creates problems for X when
not fixed (it is modified in development kernels), is
  arch/i386/kernel/ioport.c
so, unless you are running Intel kernel on your box, I fail to see how
this may affect your Alpha.

> That's why RedHat 5.1 uses
> egcs for compiling everything EXCEPT the kernels.

Compile with what you want as long as it works.  I can only tell that
personally I am, and was - for months, using multiple kernels compiled
with various versions of egcs and this was not a problem.  The same
actually goes for many people who got their machines from Hard Data.
So far I did not hear complaints that kernel does not work. :-)

  Michal

p.s. Behaviour of binaries compiled by the same version of gcc/egcs
on Intel, Alpha and other platforms can be quite different.  On the
lowest level these are not the same compilers and have private quirks.


