Dave,
	There are many differences between a noanme motherboard and a
UDB/Multia - the noname is like a 486 motherboard, it only has basic
I/O onboard (serial/parallel/floppy/IDE/SCSI) no networking, no video,
no PCMCIA, no sound... But, it does have numerous PCI and ISA slots
to add these pieces, while a UDB only has one PCI slot, unless they
jammed a 3 1/2" hard drive inside the unit.

	Don't get me wrong, a UDB is good, and a noname is good, but,
at least for me, they are not equivilent - except for performance.

Ken
khansen@njcc.com

