On Fri, 5 Jun 1998 james@maths.ex.ac.uk wrote:

> Ive seen a couple of people mention using dec fortran under linux.
> Would someone like to give me a few pointers on how one would go about
> this?

There's not a lot to it. Log into a DU box. Compile your code as you would
would normally but add the switch -non_shared, then run the binary on your
Linux box. Run-time fortran90 errors can be a problem because the compiled
code assumes there's an error message file on the system. I'm not sure
it's legal to take a copy of that, but it /might/ just work, who knows?

Ian




