>>> Mark Conway Wirt said:
> 
> Don't know too much about egcs (I've upgraded to it via RedHat 5.1, but
> I've been too busy to do much with it yet), but with my UDB/TGA I need to
> modify my XFree86.config file whenever I switch kernels, even though it's
> the same kernel, same compiler (gcc), but different patch sets.  Seems
> that the BaseMemAddress (this is from memory, might be MemBaseAddress ?)
> changes for different kernels, so I have to put a different value (from
> /proc/pci) in when I boot with different kernels.

This change of BaseMemAddress is *NOT* an EGCS side effect; it is caused by
the use of different kernel sources/patches/binaries. The addresses assigned
by the Alpha PCI bus probe/setup code have changed over time, for various
reasons.

At one time, the XFree86 XF86_TGA didn't need the MemBase option at all,
IIRC. I don't know what changed to cause the need for it to come back... :-\

--Jay++

