The firmware to run ARC is on DEC's ftp site.  The instructions are as
follows:

OKay, go to ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/, and browse down
to find the file as200_v6_7.exe.  You need to update your BIOS to this
anyway for Linux.  Also, look for a file mkboot.exe.  mkboot will take
as200_v6_7.exe and turn it into a floppy image, and then write that image to
a floppy disk (dd it basically).  Once that's done, you can then use the
command boot dva0, or whatever your floppy is, and it will boot into the
BIOS update.  If you type "update" at the Apm-> prompt (Apu->), it will
update your BIOS as it is, if you type update arc, it will switch you to ARC
console, if you type "update srm", it will update you to SRM console.  If
you switch to ARC Console, you will need to make a separate MS DOS floppy,
and simply copy as200_v6_7.exe to it, then go to the submenu to Install
firmware update..., follow the same Apu-> instructions as above to update to
whatever console.  Pain in my ass, because I couldn't find good
documentation on that.

