Nope. They have made this very clear, on many occasions.
The license is "per CPU" meaning you need to buy an OSFbase per CPU.
Sitewide agreements generally cover such things as media and doc kits,
layered prodcuts as specified int he contract, etc.. NOT CPU licenses for
OSF-base.
  It may be possible that DEC did one special for NASA, but I would check
first..

Putting it another way:
I doubt there is any opportunity to sell you a license, so I don't care
much, but in the immortal words of Robert Heinlein "TANSTAAFL" ( There
Ain't No Such Thing As A Free Lunch).

I now cease to discuss this, as I am neither a lawyer, nor did I ever want
to be one.



