Rasmol is an excellent free-ware molecular visualization program. I was
able to compile and run it under redhat 4.2 with a termino->terminos
header file change but under 5.1 it chokes under expansion of FD_SET and
FD_CLR macros. 

The following is a code snipit from the file rasmol.c.
 

static struct fd_set OrigWaitSet;
 
static int OpenConnection( socket )
    int socket;
{
    register int i;
         
    for( i=0; i<MaxConvNum; i++ )
        if( !ConvData[i].protocol )
        {   FD_SET(socket,&OrigWaitSet);
            if( socket >= WaitWidth )
                WaitWidth = socket+1;

            ConvData[i].protocol = ProtoRasMol;
            ConvData[i].socket = socket;
            return( True );
        }

    close( socket );
    return( False );
}

When doing an xmkmf and make

gcc -O2     -I/usr/X11R6/include -I/include  -Dlinux -D__alpha__
-D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=199309L -D_POSIX_SOURCE -D_XOPEN_SOURCE=500L
-D_BSD_SOURCE -D_SVID_SOURCE   -DFUNCPROTO=15 -DNARROWPROTO
-DRASMOLDIR=\"/usr/X11R6/lib/rasmol/\" -DEIGHTBIT   -c rasmol.c -o
rasmol.o

The compiler complains: 

rasmol.c: In function `OpenConnection':
rasmol.c:328: invalid use of undefined type `struct fd_set'

and 

rasmol.c: At top level:
rasmol.c:111: storage size of `OrigWaitSet' isn't known

When I explicitly include <sys/select.h> which defines fd_set the messages
still appear.
 
Have the necessary header files changed from 4.2?

If anyone wants to take a look at the code it can be found at 

http://evolution.bmc.uu.se/~thomas/mol_linux/rasmol/

Thanks,

Tim
