> IMHO time should better be used to write a new browser from scratch.
I respect that sentiment, it often seems easier to start new than to
try to learn (and fix) someone else's code - but there is a significant
investment in man-hours needed to produce all the functionality of
mozilla (browser + HTML editor + mail + news). I think it's easier to
try to port something that works. Maybe mozilla is not a good candidate
to use as a start - but I haven't seen any other "working" browsers
that have the same capability. Of the "working" browsers, I have tried
"mMosaic" and "chimera". I tried to port "amaya" - but it's even worse
