I'm not sure that speed is a real issue, but reliability definitely is.
Some may see mozilla as overkill, but it does try to provide a full set
of features for internet access - all in a single package with a consistent
user interface. (I'm not trying to defend or promote mozilla here, I'm
simply trying to point out what I consider its good points).

> Mozilla converts pointers to integers all the time, which shows the
