I believe most of the Xlib stuff had the same problem, but it now works
(more or less) for alpha - but you're right - the best way to get rid
of the pointer/int conversion is to rewrite big parts of the code and
change data structures that store pointers to have those defined as
pointers, not ints.

I'm starting to think it would be better to focus on getting a full
Java implementation for LinuxAlpha, then using Java versions of browser,
mail/news clients, etc. For those of us who want to use mozilla, there
is a Java rewrite underway, but there are other Java-based tools which
should run with a full LinuxAlpha Java implementation.

