It's not futile, you've just had two strikes against you from the start:

1. your box is equipped with a 24-plane TGA, aka ZLXp-E2,
2. MILO's 24-plane TGA support is (or was :-) broken.

The -E2 and -E3 have been problematic for quite a long time, but, since there
aren't many of them out there, it's not been a problem (squeaky wheels, you
know :-).

Most of the time, the solution adopted has been to simply replace that TGA
with a standard VGA of some type; Millennium, or S3 of some flavor, or ATI,
are common choices.

Also, it's quite possible that if you'd been running SRM console, that the
avanti-s.img would have worked well enough for you, as the kernel TGA support
is (nearly) up to the task of running on an -E2 or -E3.

Anyway, all that aside, I'll be putting a new AVANTI MILO image with vastly
improved 24-plane TGA support, out on gatekeeper.dec.com at:

	/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/milo-avanti-980606

Look for it there sometime tomorrow (Sunday), as it takes a while for it
to be mirrored off my local server.

Good luck, let me know if you have any problems with it.

Oh, and remember, there's currently no XFree86 support under LINUX for the
24-plane TGAs, so you may want to consider the VGA after all...

--Jay++

