On 07-Jun-98 Don Crimbchin wrote:
> I'm running into a problem trying to compile GTK.
> When I run the configure script, I get the following:

<snip>

> checking host system type... Invalid configuration
> `alphapca56-unknown-linux-gnu': machine `alphapca56-unknown' not
> recognized

<snip>

> ltconfig: you must specify a host type if you use `--no-verify'
> Try `ltconfig --help' for more information.
> configure: error: libtool configure failed

I've run into this many times. I'd guess you're using an SX164 system. The
21164PC CPU reports itself as 21164pca56 instead of the 21164ev56 which the
21164a does.

I solved the problem by changing the two references to 21164ev56 in config.sub
to 21164pca56. This allowed things to proceed and I've not yet had problems with
the resulting code, although I've not tried GTK. It did work fine with KDE, EGCS
and other programs using auto-config.

Somebody should update the auto-config stuff to include the SX processor I
guess.

---
Brian E.W. Wood  beww@intac.com


