Yup...  I didn't even get a floppy with my UDB...
Iwas pleasently surprised when I was able to install it on my alpha.  I
got the alpha not even knowing what the hecka  UDB was...  I baught it
because I knew alphas were cool and for $225 over a year ago it is still
to this day a good deal...  I got realy lucky!
I had isntalled slackwere on a deckstation 486 and redhat intel on my
p-166 but never gone beyond an install...
I got multia crap on my machine and used it for a little while...  I
noticed that an 8 cd set I had said that it had linux for alphas...  I
cheacked around and found that install was going to be hard w/o a
floppy...  Here are my steps:
Copy milo and linload.exe to the hard drive on a small fat partition (done
under NT or on another system)
Boot milo
Boot live filesystem from the redhat cd (boot -t iso9660
scd0:/kernels/noname.gz root=/dev/scd0)
do the install...
Simple and quick...  though you do need another scsi machine or nt on the
alpha...


