> installed off of it? If not does anyone have the proper way to move the
> dirs too , or if someone has the Alpha 5.1 Redhat cdrom could they possibly
> give me the dir trees? I would like any comments or questions, Also i am

Though I havn't tried it with 5.1, what you basically need to do is
this: Grab the misc/source/trees/boot stuff directly from
ftp.redhat.com using the on-the-fly tar facility. I.e. use 
'get boot.tar' to download the boot Directory and anything below. This
makes sure the the device entries in /dev will be correct. That's
usually the thing that's different on the mirrors.

Other than that use common sense to determine what else you will
need. If the CD should be bootable from the SRM console, you need to
apply 'isomarkboot' from the 'aboot' Package. Note that this only
works with CD drives that are capable of 512 byte block sizes. 

HTH, Martin
