Well, I love my Alpha 21164, but it locks up every 20-30 hours.  I have a
redhat 5.0 install, with 2.1.103 running as my kernel.

The lockup is more of a hang.  The system responds to pings, when I telnet
to it, the port opens and just sits there.  The console is also frozen,
but on carrage return it does goto a new line.

If I do a warm reboot, (just drop back into milo, and reload the box)
everything is fine for another 20 hours or so.  If I let it run, I will be
100% sure it will crash.

There is nothing in the logs.. the logs just stop. 

I've done everything I can think of.  I have changed almost every chunk of
hardware in the system, and no matter what I do.. its unstable.

I had the real-time clock problem, and changed milo that fixed the clock,
and I had some ide problems also.  I dumped ide, and moved on to scsi..
thinking that was my problem.

I've tested DE500/Intel Pro10/100 NIC's, I have tested diff video cards.

I need some help.  I am about to the point where I can't use the system,
and I am going to buy a (gag me) intel PII system to replace my alpha.

Hardware:
The system is a 533MHz 21164sx. 
Corsair memory 128 megs
Adaptech 2940uw controller
UW SCSI drives
no ide/no floppy
3com 509 tpo NIC

Any ideas would be great!!

-Barrett Lyon


