Hello:

I just moved my Alpha XL 233 from 4 x 8 Mb tin-contact SIMMS for a total
of 32 Mb to 2 x 32 Mb gold-contact plus 4 x 8 Mb tin-contact for a new
total of 96 Mb.  The combination seems to work fine, and my Linux box is
now #@$(&* *&^*@ (&@# fast!!!  :^)

I was just wondering if this is an acceptable thing to do in the Alpha
world.  I'm under the understanding that in the Intel world, mixing gold &
tin can lead to corrosion (not that I've ever seen it happen in real
life), and more importantly, the mixed RAM can lead to software failure.

The system is *SO* nice now.  What a difference an extra 64 Mb can make!

