On Mon, 8 Jun 1998, Barrett G. Lyon wrote:

> Well, I love my Alpha 21164, but it locks up every 20-30 hours.  I have a
> redhat 5.0 install, with 2.1.103 running as my kernel.

With the experimental kernels, you can get some system info by hitting the
<alt>-<SysReq>-* keys, though I don't know if this works on alpha.
Presumably you can switch vt's, and if so, what I like to do is put this
entry in my inittab:

cc:1235:respawn:/usr/bin/top -s < /dev/tty12 > /dev/tty12 2>&1

Then hit <Alt>-<F12> whenever you want to see what's going on.  This may
or may not help you with your problem.  Handy either way. 

At times, though, I think it may cause problems of its own, though this is
pure conjecture.  Once every couple weeks when I notice the CPU time
climbing into the multiple thousands, I'll hit 'q', and init will respawn
it.  You can use this as an additional test of init...

