On Thursday,  4 Jun, Colin Coller wrote:
> 
> I'm having problems with sound support on my UDB.  It works, but when
> sound support initializes, it hisses loudly until something is sent to
> /dev/dsp.  Has anyone else experienced this?

Is it an AD1845 chip?  (cat /dev/sndstat, look for `Audio devices')

If yes, you can try the following patch.  (Provided that you haven't
applied it already, as it is, to the best of my knowledge, part of Jay's
alpha-patches.)

	Nikita


--- linux/drivers/sound/ad1848.c.orig	Sat Aug 30 21:01:15 1997
+++ linux/drivers/sound/ad1848.c	Sun Sep  7 03:53:37 1997
@@ -1145,7 +1145,7 @@
     0x00, 0x0c, 0x02, 0x00, 0x8a, 0x01, 0x00, 0x00,
 
   /* Positions 16 to 31 just for CS4231/2 and ad1845 */
-    0x80, 0x00, 0x10, 0x10, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,
+    0x80, 0x00, 0x10, 0x10, 0x00, 0x00, 0x1f, 0x40,
     0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00
   };
 


