Er, well, you won't be able to build a new MILO under 5.0 that will work...
Kernels, yes, but the best MILOs use the DEC BIOS emulator, which is a C++
binary built under 4.2, and it has problems linking with the 5.0 binaries.

I don't have a good solution for you at this time; I've not built a MIATA
kernel or MILO for a while, so it'll take a bit of doing (backport of the
patch to 2.0.30 which is the last kernel source to be known to work for the
building of MILO).

I'll try to get around to doing the port/build tonight, but can't promise
I'll get it done for tomorrow...

BTW, here's what I'm going to put into my patches for qlogicisp.c, so that
the detection/work-around is automatic:

#if RELOAD_FIRMWARE
#if defined(__alpha__)
	/* do not reload firmware if 1040B, ie revision 5 chip */
	if (((struct isp1020_hostdata *) host->hostdata)->revision == 5)
		printk("qlogicisp: 1040B detected, no firmware reload.\n");
	else
#endif /* __alpha__ */

--Jay++

