At work we have SunOS and Solaris, so my config file has stuff to
determine which OS the machine I'm logged into is running, then set
PATH, etc. accordingly.

To get this to work in your environment you need to find common commands
that tell you what OS and CPU you're logged into - e.g. mach,arch,uname
and set PATH, TERM, etc. accordingly.

Of course, if you're using different shells on different machines, then you
have more than 1 set of config files to deal with.

Larry Z.



