It is likely that you are overdriving the monitor.
That is too say the pixel rate,, or vertical refresh numbers are too high
for it to display.
Be very careful. Many monitors can be damaged or even totally trashed by
being overdriven. Repair bill can be more than teh cost of a 14" monitor.
If you see this "no picture" condition, I suggest IMMEDIATELY powering off
the monitor, doing the CTRL-ALT-Backspace, and then turning the monitor
back on.




