> I have the software raid working with 2.1.101 but seem to have hit my 
> head when trying to get a root file system to be raid1. It looks as 
> though initrd is not supported by milo or the alpha verion of linux.

Perhaps I'm missing something, but doesn't it go like this:

1) linload loads milo from a FAT filesystem
2) Milo reads a kernel off any filesystem it understands, and passes
   it arguments
3) that kernel reads the root filesystem off anything it understands

With this existing setup, you can have your root filesystem on raid1
-- you just can't make milo read the kernel off a mirrored
disk. That's a 99% solution for most people; a running system will
survive a disk failure, but may not be able to reboot.

initrd in the kernel wouldn't help you; initrd in milo would get the
other 1%.

-- g


