I probably found the reason why Richard's egcs-1.0.3a is able to compile
mm/page_alloc.o while mine exits with a signal 6. The RedHat spec file, 
from which I've built my egcs, enables three options (--enable-shared, 
--enbale-haifa and --enable-threads).  I've rebuilt egcs without these 
options, and I'm now able to compile page_alloc without failure. As my
Noname isn't the fastest machine, maybe someone with a faster Alpha can
narrow down, which of the options triggers the problem.

Richard, which options did you use to build your egcs ?

Thomas.

