I believe this helped me of a sorts.

I compiled the 2.1.105 kernel (after I commented out the SMP=1 line in the
/usr/src/linux/Makefile) without a hitch.  

It appears to work; however the loader segfaults everytime I try to start
Netscape. :(  em86 complains about missing two libraries when I try to run
the x86 version of Netscape.  So both options still aren't working, but I
will keep plugging at it.

[root@malcolm netscape]# ./netscape
2456:/sbin/loader: Fatal Error: loader cannot be invoked directly 
Segmentation fault

Using the new kernel DID fix a significant problem I had
with NFS mounting a Solaris 2.5.1 box that is being tested as a NFS-DFS
gateway.  Before (2.0.34 kernel), I would get: 

?--------- 3 root root 2048 <date> /...

Now it behaves as a proper directory. :)

So I have to say thanks to the list, especially Alexandre.  The NASA
Technical Coordinator I work with is currently installing a 4 gig SCSI
drive so he can install Linux on his x86 box...thanks again.


