world?  Linux is starting to get recognition as being a very viable
solution for corporate computing finally, but they vendors are really
embarassing it.  My boss wants product X and I have to tell him (a) I
don't know the price, they don't send e-mails or return calls (b) I don't
know the delivery time, it could be a week or 2 months.

