This posting is in lue with the syslogd "stuff".  Reading the archives of
this list, I have seen a lot of people have the syslogd problems (as do
I).  My problem is where syslogd uses up massave resources, and then uses
all the file handles up on the machine, then the machine crashes.  I don't
think it is caused by syslogd.  I might be way off here, but I feel that
it is caused by wu-ftpd.  I have noticed wu-ftpd sometimes gets stuck as
user root, and starts using up cpu and memory at huge rate.  Somehow I
feel that ftpd is causing syslogd to have some problems. The second I
removed ftpd from inetd, my machine has not crashed.  I am not the best in
this area, but I think that something is going on, has anyone had this
problem also?

-Barrett


