I had this problem with the ftpd that ships with RedHat5.0.  Whenever a
login failed or a client bailed out, the server went through the roof.
I compiled a fresh wu-ftpd on the box and the problem dissapeared.  I
would recommend you try the same and see if the machine still crashes
with ftpd on, and doesn't with ftpd off.  I'd be interested to hear the
results.  (Can't test it here.  The main ftp server is the Alpha box
that had the problem.)

BTW, what kernel version are you running?

