>> i/o addresses. 
>
>I had no idea bout that... Hmm.. But then, how does one know what address
>to use...?
>

A parallel or serial chip will have a set of pins that are used to tell it
what information you are putting or requesting on the data pins. It is very
similar to a memory chip if you know about address decoding there; just a
smaller 'footprint'.

Systems developers and hardware manufacturers usually map these to a base
address with the rest being in the logical order specified in the chip specs,
but it might not be so, therefore you just have to hope that they all comply
to the same idea, or read the relevant documentation for the machine/card. 

Alan


