Sorry Larry.
We received 7 serious enquiries / commitments to this suggetion.
As I originally said, with a quick run at my adding machine I figured it
would take 10 machines or more to make it a break-even proposition at the
price I suggested.

Bottom line is it turned out to be much less of a desirable ting than it
seemed at first blush. I was tired of all the UDB heat, UDB "where do I put
a disk" type questions and proposed this. I was actually hoping for about
20 or more, then I could actually make a few dollars at this. Not much, but
at least enough to pay for my time in doing it.

I think the thing is that so many good cheap Alpha boxes are out there now
that people are living with it until they buy their next Alpha, or they
already bought something.

Another issue is probably with the flawed level of RH 5 and 5.1, we
probably have seen most of the "lower-end" users on UDB's drop out of Alpha
Linux. To have a working Linux Alpha at that level you either are willing
to spend quite a bit of time working out the bugs, or have a vendor who
will provide it that way and support it. AS UDB's are all cheap surplus
boxes, there ain't much support.

Pity..

Anyway, bottom line is still that it will cost about $600 for me to get 10
built, or about $800 for 25, or $1000 for 50, and so on..

If 5 people still want to do it for $120 each fine, although it strikes me
as too pricey at that level.



