We are talking about the problems people experience with egcs-1.0.2 from
RedHat 5.1 and self built egcs-1.0.3a with the RedHat .spec file. There seems
to be at least one bug left, when --enable-haifa is given at configure time
(at that's what the RedHat .spec file does). With haifa enabled there is
one file in the 2.1 kernel, which can't be compiled (mm/page_alloc.c).
And Richard guesses that this compiler bug might also be responsable for
the X problems in 5.1. So we are suggesting to put out an updated RPM for
egcs without --enable-haifa.

