Dear Jokke,

> Speaking of this, has anybody noticed that make config, make menuconfig
> and make xconfig gives you different options?  In my case, I use
> menuconfig or xconfig, and then I take a special look at .config
> manually, to turn on support for my scsi-card.

For a while the message has been "don't use make {menu,x}config, use plain
make config".

There was a patch for a while that fixed it, sort of, but it remains true.

If you have used make {menu,x}config then the only safe route in my
experience (with 2.0.33 and 2.1.103) is to "make mrproper; make config"
which means reentering all the right options sequentially.  Sorry.  It is
easier if you first print out the .config that sort of worked (because
"make mrproper" will remove it).

> I don't see this as a real problem; I know what to do, and so on, but it
> is quite bad... .. I don't know what's causing this or what's actually
> happening... :(

I agree: it is bad.

Cheers,
	Kristoffer

