Subject: Announcement 2 - linload source now available
To: axp-list@redhat.com
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: TEXT/plain; CHARSET=US-ASCII

The boot sequence for Linux/Alpha from the ARC console or AlphaBIOS
includes a module called "linload.exe".  This is a small program
that runs in the ARC/AlphaBIOS environment which is used to load
MILO.

Until now, I have not been able to release the source for linload.exe
because it was built against a firmware development toolkit that was
only available under Microsoft NDA.  I was not certain of the legal
status of source which included calls to the firmware routines.

Recently, though, a subset of the firmware kit, called the "ARC
Application Development Kit" has been made generally available.
I have modified linload to build against this kit, and the sources
are now available.  You can find them in

	ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/linload

The sources are in "linload.zip" or "linload.tar.gz", and instructions
for building linload are in the README file.  You need to build it
on a Windows NT system, and you need Microsoft Visual C++ 4.1 along
with the Windows NT SDK and DDK in order to build it.  The README file
also includes instructions for downloading the ARC development kit.

Have fun!

-- 
