> Hi,
> Does anyone know if StorageWorks is compatible with RH5.1, if not can
> software raid be made to work with StorageWorks subsystem?
> TIA
> Kokan

	The Digital StorageWorks repertoire is many things, what
	exactly do you mean ?

	Originally it was nice mechanics for semi-hot-pluggable SCSI
	buss(es).  Then the repertoire got various RAID controllers
	to be used between the host interface bus, and the SCSI busses.

	If you consider HRZ40* series controllers, the host-side is
	SCSI bus (wide differential), which means that any system is
	able to use it (if you have applicable host adapter.)
	(ftp.funet.fi uses this type of controller to handle 120 GB of
	 its circa 170 GB of anonymous FTP storage space.)
	Those are high-end devices, which also means their price is
	not very low, but their performance certainly is nice :-)

	If you consider "low-end" host-based raid-controllers,
	then the Mylex device is the one you are interested in,
	but it has no ready-to-run driver so far in pre-packaged
	distributions.  Live in bleeding-edge, or come back in
	about years time.

/Matti Aarnio <mea@nic.funet.fi> <matti.aarnio@sonera.fi>


