> and takes up two PCI slots , has its own fans and 32MB of
> RAM  and I think we could create some nice graphics with
> this)

This board is your problem; it has a builtin CIRRUS VGA plus an accelerator
chipset. Only the latest MILO knows how to deal with the CIRRUS (if you enable
it's BIOS, that disables its memory; go figure), so try the one for RH 5.1,
or grab a copy off gatekeeper.dec.com:

	/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/milo-miata-980609

You could also try the MIATA kernel that's there, too: miata-kernel-2034.gz

Note that neither XFree86 nor any of the commercial Xserver houses supports
that card under Linux/Alpha, AFAIK; at best you'll have console text mode
working, and that's it.

> I replaced PowerStorm with some other card. This card is one
> piece, altough it takes up two slots. I accessed
> Alpha BIOS , PCI configurataion I found this two lines:
> 
>   DEVICE NAME                           DEVICE TYPE
> Ven ID=1013, DevID=a0                      VGA
> Ven ID=1091, DevID=e4                       Video card

I think this is another Powerstorm ofd some flavor, as 1013/a0 is CIRRUS 5430.

Try a standard VCGA of some sort; Millennium, S3, ATI are all known to work.

--Jay++

