>>> peter.mcdonald@afp.gov.au said:
> 
> I am trying to install Redhat 5.0 (from the Powertools 6-CD set) on a DEC 2100
> Alphaserver, 1x 200MHz CPU, and 384 Mb RAM. 
> 
> I have tried using both SRM with aboot, and ARC with MILO. 

There is no MILO support for the SABLE family (2000/2100 but NOT 2100A).

You must boot from SRM console; RH has sable-s.img floppy image files under
4.2, 5.0, and/or 5.1, IIRC. Follow the appropriate SRM booting directions
from the FAQ. Be sure to partition your harddisk with BSD-style partition
table (use the "b" option under fidks), and leave 1024 sectors at the front
for installation of the bootstrap (aboot).

Good luck.

