> else have this problem?
>
> What does it mean and how can I fix it?

	unset LC_CTYPE

In the GLIBC there is weird code within the locale handling, and
frankly I am not sure WHO should fix what.  Linux/Alpha knows
about _MAP_INHERIT flag, but does not support it!

I think it used to be with name:  MAP_INHERIT  in the headers, and maybe
as such did cause early injection of the flag into GLIBC 2.0 sources ?

Another way to silence it is to go and edit your kernel; that report is
generated in  arch/alpha/kernel/osf_sys.c
Comment out the test and printk() giving that message.

