>>> Martin Hxy said:
> 
> I just downloaded the alpha-patches for 2.0.34 and applied them to a
> vanilla 2.0.34. It compiled on my pws433a with a few warnings and
> seems to work.
> 
> The only suspicious thing is that when I boot the machine, I get these
> messages (output from dmesg):
> 
> 
> qlogicisp : new isp1020 revision ID (5)
> qlogicisp : 1040B detected, no firmware reload

This indicates a QLogic controller with a 1040B, which sometimes has a problem
with the default firmware in the LINUX driver (qlogicisp.c). Make sure that you
have the very latest AlphaBIOS console code, to ensure the latest firmware has
already been downloaded to the controller *before* MILO starts, *AND* that you
have the very latest MIATA MILO from gatekeeper.dec.com:

	/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/milo-miata-980609

> Partition check:
>  sda:kernel: unaligned trap at fffffc00003aaf94: fffffc00000541be 28 1
> kernel: unaligned trap at fffffc00003aafa8: fffffc00000541c2 28 2
>  sda1 sda2 sda3 sda4
> 
> I'm not sure whether this is a problem or not, but I would like to
> know what these errors mean.

What kind of partition table do you have on /dev/sda? Sometimes the DOS style
partition tables have caused this message to appear. Don't worry about it, as
they are just warnings, everything is working OK.

--Jay++

