>>> Veraldi Center for Educational Technology said:
> 
> I'm trying to get RH 4.2 up on a Alpha Xl266... I have 2 problems:
> Number one, MILO doesn't see the SCSI drives.  (I do have the latest MILO
> from  gatekeeper.dec.com).

Just to check, that MILO would be:

	/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/Test-Milos-2.0.30+/xl

right? Or the XL MILO from either RH 5.0 or 5.1 would do, they are all
identical.

> The errors end with:
> "Cache Incorrectly Configured". (The errors fly by quite quickly.)

This indicates a problem with configuration of the SCSI controller; I've
seen those messages before, when something in the PCI probing/setup was not
correct.

> The second problem (and not my choice) is that I have a Millinium II 
> video card.  When I start X, originally, the system hangs.  I can't find a way
> to get any output fron the server (to be saved, anyway).  So I tried the 
> "no_pci_disconnect" option, and since then I get an error (yes, I get output
> now)  to the effect of 
> 
>     Fatal server error:
>     xf86EnableIOPorts: Failed to set IOPL for I/O
> 
> 
> I still get this error even though I took out the "no_pci_disconnect" option.
> This, I looks to me like a hardware error, but NT still works on this box, as
> does Linux from the console.

A number of comments:

1. the "no_pci_disconnect" option is only implemented in the S3/S3V servers

2. Mill II should best be run using the 3.3.2 release of XFree86

3. you want to put a "VideoMem xxxx" option in the Device section, with the
   correct amount of video RAM; seems that the Mill II can hang a system when
   initially probing for how much video memory is present, and supplying the
   amount avoids the problem.

4. you MUST be running an XL kernel, *NOT* an AVANTI one, especially when
   attempting to use a Millennium of any flavor.

5. you must do exactly the following:

	ln -s Avanti /etc/alpha_systype

   in order for GLIBC to know what type of system you have. Recent (5.0 update
   and 5.1) GLIBC's should support XL without that link, but YMMV...

Good luck.

--Jay++

