Content-Type: TEXT/PLAIN; charset=US-ASCII


We need to be filled in on what they are working on for the Alphas!  I
have no idea if I am ever going to see my kernel 2.1.99 compile without me
compiling egcs-1.0.3a.  Or if I will ever be able to compile mySQL again.
We need a web page (probably run by RedHat people) that we can submit
problems to so they know what problems are still occuring.  For instance I
am STILL seeing people complain about "man" seg faulting, when there is
clearly a new man*.alpha.rpm in the updates directory on Redhat/mirrors
this needs to stop!  Let the RH/Alpha people read something that means
something.

We need a list of issues that haven't been solved, like:
	egcs new RPM (getting contrib/i386 fixed my mySQL compile problems)
	compiling kernel 2.0.34 and 2.1.90+ issues (need new egcs?)
	ipfwadm has a socket option error given the right parameter
	ntpd problems?  I have not verified this...

Maybe these have all been solved!?  But how do I know this?  I try to
read the majority of the posts, but it would be much nicer to have a
"leader board of bugs" that we can look at.  If a person has a problem
that is not fixed by the errata and not on the "leader board of bugs" then
he/she should submit a bug report to the board.  If it is found that it is
legitimate problem it should be added to the board.

I'm all for compiling programs for myself, but I feel I shouldn't be
replacing broken rpm packages with source I compile.  It defeats the
purpose of rpms.

/end of soapbox

Here I go, off to compile egcs-1.0.3a on my UDB for the next couple hours.  

Thanks for listening,
-Scott


