Just like in audio where 16-bits of the "right" resolution would be enough, 
but digital doesn't give it to you, 24 bit color doesn't always work.  This of 
it this way: For any given color you only really have 256 shades.  If you do 
X-ray imaging in a medical enviroment then you are going to want more 
resolution.  There are a number of other areas were this is true.  The most 
common fix is to use 30 bit color instead of 24 bit color which gives ~4k 
shades.


