Since there seems to be interest,

> I suspect it's called "True Color"
> because some marketing genius thought it would make the boxes get off
> the shelves faster.

This is a bit pessimistic -- but generally true  :-).  It's called true
color at 8 bits per shade (red, green, blue, or whatever palate you choose)
the human eye cannot distinguish between adjacent colors.  There is a bit
of literature on this, it is interesting seeing the 5, 6, 7, and 8 bit
spectra of a single color or shades of grey presented.  Only the 8 bit
spectrum appears continuous.

Of course, it is only "true color" under inspection by the human eye.

