>>> Richie Crews said:
> OK now i got it installed, now i got the milo prompt, i tried the noname.gz
> from redhat's site. No luck it stops at switching memory address. Then i
> tried avanti-s.gz and it says request blah 0 over and over again. Any idea
> what kernel image i should use for a Alpha station 4/166 and can someone
> give me a command line and the way to copy it to the disk and the milo boot
> command line?

OK, an AS200 4/166 is a member of the AVANTI family, *but*, since you are
booting from MILO, avanti-s.img is inappropriate, since that is to be used
*only* when booting directly from SRM console (hence the "-s" in the name,
courtesy of the gremlins at Red Hat :-).

You want to use the "xl.img"; an XL is an AVANTI one-off (not a member of
the family, actually, since there are some additional HW limitations on XL
that aren't on AVANTI); however, an AVANTI will work with those limitations,
so we consolidate kernels.

Good luck.

--Jay++

