One gig is quite small by today standards.  Recently we were formatting
much bigger partitions without any incidents.  This is 2.0.30, right?


Try 'echo  ".... " > /proc/sys/vm/freepages' where .... stands for a
triplet of numbers which are at least twice the size of what you will
get doing 'cat /proc/sys/vm/freepages'.  Maybe even more than double.
I thought that a need for that hack is already gone in 2.0.30.
OTOH I run 2.0.33 immediately after I was able to boot for the first
time.

You may try to leave /home alone for a time beeing.  Install, make
yourself a decent kernel and run mk2efs on this partition then.

Michal

