Richie,

Bad news.  From what I read, TGA 24 plane video card is *NOT* yet supported for
X.

If you are using ARC and you haven't installed the linux system on /dev/sda2,
then most probably you don't have vmlinux.gz on that partition.  So you should
delete the osloadoptions line from you boot menu.  If you reboot now you'll come
to the MILO> prompt.  At the prompt, type
	boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1
Of course you should put the disk containing the file 'vmlinux.gz' in the floppy
drive.  

The question is, if you can't run X, is it worth the trouble in installing
linux?

Regards,
Weiping

