I know we're all on budgets here, but RAM is cheap these days.  And swapping
is sssssllllooooowwwww.  I paid $104 to add 64Mb RAM to my UDB, and turned it
from a slug to a reasonable machine - mostly because it *never* swaps except
under extreme loads.  If you've got a few bucks, RAM is the best speed upgrade
for the lowest cost.

