I have been running virtual domains for the past 9 months with no
difficulties...until about 3 weeks ago.  At that time, the virtuals (6 of
them, now) began to display erratically.  One time part of them would answer
and the others would time out or fail to answer...then a few minutes later
the one answering would stop and some of the others would then answer.
Rarely would all of them answer in the same session.  In the last few days,
this behavior has degraded to only a couple answering and now, none will
answer.

Has anyone else run into this?  I've gone through the config files to make
sure nothing has changed.  I've uninstalled Apache 1.2.5-1 (RedHat--Alpha)
and re-installed an earlier version -- 1.2.4-4...and set up the virtuals
again.  Didn't help a bit....they still don't answer.

If anyone has any ideas....please!  Right now I'm at wits-end on what to do
next.

Alpha UDB
64MB memory
128MB Swap
RedHat 5.0
Apache 1.2.4-4 (currently -- about to upgrade to 1.2.5-1 again)

Thanks!
Frank



