I have an AlphaStation 200 4/233.
I am trying to get RedHat 5.1 to autoboot from the SRM. To do this, I
need to run swriteboot to install bootlx... It's all in the install
manual.
	So anyway, I've tried a couple of scenarios:

	1) created a 2mb partition as sda1 to gibe it room.   

No good. running /sbin/swriteboot -v /dev/sda /boot/bootlx destroyed the
partition table leaving only partition sda1 & sda2. all others were
gone.  So I re-installed 5.1, and tried this (per the manual)

	Leave a 2mb space at the begining of the disk to give space for bootlx.
... ok.
	So I started sda1 at sector 4 (rather than the usual sector 1). When
the install finished, I ran swriteboot again, and "bam" partition table
blown again.

	I'm tired of re-installing this thing now, so I thought I'd check to
see what others are doing this. Could someone send along how they've set
up the opening partitions to allow swriteboot to do it's thing?

	Thank you in advance. I'm getting frustrated beyond belief with this!


			Thanks again!

				Ric


