I successfully installed a 2.0.34 kernel on an LX164 using the patches at
gatekeeper.dec.com
    /pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/alpha-patches-2.0.34-0.1.gz

I'm using the 2.6n ncr53c8xx driver and version 0.89H of tulip without any 
problems so far. 

One note:  there were still some unresolved dependency problems with nfs. 
Below is a patch posted to linux.dev.kernel in 1997 which seems to solve
the problem.

>Subject:      Patch against 2.0.29 - arch/alpha/kernel/ksyms.c
>From:         econommx@rose-hulman.edu (Matthew X. Economou)
>Date:         1997/03/14
>Message-ID:   <w4on2s5ygct.fsf@nemesis.economou.org>
>Newsgroups:   linux.dev.kernel

>When compiling on the Alpha (I don't know if this problem occurs on
>other architectures), the following modules have unresolved
>dependencies in the stock 2.0.29 kernel:

>        - binfmt_aout: start_thread
>        - isofs: strncat
>        - slhc: ip_fast_csum
>        - nfs: __kernel_thread

>The following patch (created with 'diff -u3 ...') to
>arch/alpha/kernel/ksyms.c appears to fix these dependencies.

--- linux/arch/alpha/kernel/ksyms.c.mxe Fri Mar 14 17:38:40 1997
+++ linux/arch/alpha/kernel/ksyms.c     Fri Mar 14 17:44:57 1997
@@ -12,7 +12,10 @@
 #include <linux/elfcore.h>
 #include <asm/io.h>
 #include <asm/hwrpb.h>
+#include <asm/processor.h>
+#include <asm/checksum.h>
 
+extern long __kernel_thread(unsigned long, int (*)(void *), void *);
 extern void bcopy (const char *src, char *dst, int len);
 extern struct hwrpb_struct *hwrpb;
 
@@ -62,6 +65,7 @@
        X(strcmp),
        X(strcpy),
        X(strlen),
+       X(strncat),
        X(strncmp),
        X(strncpy),
        X(strnlen),
@@ -76,7 +80,10 @@
        X(dump_thread),
        X(dump_fpu),
        X(hwrpb),
+       X(ip_fast_csum), /* slhc */
        X(wrusp),
+       X(start_thread), /* binfmt_aout */
+       X(__kernel_thread), /* nfs */
 
        /*
         * The following are special because they're not called




