	cp -ax

       -a, --archive
              Preserve  as  much as possible of the structure and
              attributes of the original files in the copy.   The
              same as -dpR.

       -x, --one-file-system
              Skip  subdirectories that are on different filesys-
              tems from the one that the copy started on.


