> Hello.
Hello!

> I have been trying to run gtk-1.0.4 based programs (gimp 1.0.0, for 
> one) on my alpha. I have compiled both from the original source codes
> using egcs (gcc version egcs-2.90.27 980315 (egcs-1.0.2 release))
> under 2.0.34.
> Now, gtk and the applications compile fine. The problem is that
> every gtk-application that uses pixmaps, aborts and shows a 
> following error message:
> ** ERROR **: BadAccess (attempt to access private resource denied)
>   serial 7668 error_code 10 request_code 129 minor_code 3
> Any comments?
Geez!
That's supposed to become a FAQ.
OK. Here is the trick. The whole thing has nothing to do with X or the
compiler. Some kernel code is broken, namely the SysV-IPC code. This causes
in general XSHM to fail with _any_ program.
Solution is to get either 2.1.10? kernel or to apply the alpha-2.0.34-?.diff
from gatekeeper (don't know the exact URL anymore).
After that everything should work fine.
CU
  nils

PS: I wonder why this patch is not in the so called 'stable' 2.0.34 kernel?



