There have been some rumours coming out on what XFree86 4.0 is about; it looks 
like it is to be a substantially more modular system.  This should help in 
allowing extensions to be closer to being "first class members."

Mind you, it's vaporware thus far, so we'll see what really happens Real Soon 
Now.  Hopefully in 1998...

> > > defaults mechanism is also needed.  There should, IMHO, be three
> > > configuration files for each program - one in .../app-defaults, one in
> > > .../app-defaults/fixed, and one in the user's home directory - just like
> > > the setup for Pine.  There should be *NO* registry.
