> It is because they aren't allowed to share.  I don't know the details of

They *ARE* allowed to share, it's just the crappy programmers at Netscape and
the crappy quality of open source (warning: flame bait) means that they don't
bother to write their code to properly share.

When I worked at GeoVision, our application initially was 8 bit color because
all the work stations of the day had 8 bits.  But then we decided we needed 4
bit planes for satellite imagery, so we reduced our code to only use 4 bit
planes.  We did a hell of a lot of work with making sharable lut (look up
table) entries, using what was there already if at all possible, dithering
when we couldn't get the colors we needed, etc, and made a *very* color
friendly system.  Fortunately we had a mad genius who wrote all this code, and
I don't know all the details of how he did it.  No private colour maps, so no
flashing, just a warning that if you started something colour intensive and
unfriendly before our software, you might get something that doesn't look
quite right.

