I think that it should be ANSI-C, yes, just like GTK+ is ANSI C and Win32
is ANSI C.  If you want C++, that's fine, use the wrappers: GTK-, MFC, ...

> Many applications don't use the color models properly.  X supports 
> pseudocolor, directcolor, truecolor, whatever... it tries hard to use the 

Perhaps another model is needed so it acts like Windows/dithering.  I
think this is the most acclimated model.

> hardware resources as best as it can.  "Colormap flashing" is a reasonable
