> There must be a HOWTO out there with some information bass-ackwards.  Try
> using the interface IP address of your EXTERNAL connection (your PPP
> device) with the -V flag, or better yet, do it like this:

as someone pointed out, there is an howto under /usr/doc/HOWTO/mini (what
makes a HOWTO mini as opposed to major?) for IP masquerading that tries to
explain all of this.  This is the broken one, as it says to have the -W or
-V option pointing to the ethernet (maqueraded network) interface.  The
man page on ipfwadm is very unclear about those two options two saying
"Optional address (or name in case of -W) of an interface via which a
packet is received, or via which is packet is going to be sent."

> ipfwadm -F -a accept -m -S 10.0.0.0/24 -W ppp0

this worked for me, thanks.  I figured it was something simple like this,
but as I had not seen any one mention IP masquerading on this list, i did
not know if anyone was using it (or if there was some problem with the
alpha port of it)

now i can be off and do more interesting things, like dial-on-demand and
setting up some proxy servers.  Thanks!

