On Wed, Jun 17, 1998 at 08:06:05AM -0500, Eric Hilton Jones wrote:
>   Does anyone know of a fortran compiler that runs under alpha linux that
> will support real*16? g77 won't do it, microway apparently won't do it,
> and the nag page is uninformative. 

To begin with, know that no Alpha can do real*16 in hardware.

But all the bits needed to emulate real*16 in software exists,
though you'd have to tweek it just a little to work with gcc.
I don't know how much tweeking you'd have to do to g77 to get
it to accept real*16.

The biggest issue is that there are no library routines extant
to deal with real*16 -- sqrt, exp and the like -- and it would
probably be a significant amount of work to write them.

As far as other alternatives, you might try the portland group.


