Sounds like you just described the X True Color visual to me, which
can be supported at 8 bits but it depends on if the X server has it
implemented that way. My Rage Pro/Mystique/Permedia cards are all
True Color when I run them at 16 bit with XFree on PPro's/Alphas.
No flashing occurs on them when I run high color apps. X has a
XGetRGBColormap/XSetRGBColormap routine to manage sharing color
maps. Most apps don't go to the trouble of using this feature though.
The routines also attach atoms to the Root window to allow you
to fetch them from any other window. They use ICCCM (Inter Client
Communication Conventions Manual) conventions when accessing the
atoms/info on the root window. So, one proposal to behave "like
Windows" would be to have the WM set up color maps for use by
all apps and then tell everyone they have to use those colormaps.
(That would float like a lead ballon)
Come to think of it, when I run Netscape and XV on the same screen
in 8 bit mode, things still don't flash. Who ever starts last just
doesn't get many colors. Are you all saying GIMP flashes?? That's
GIMP's problem then...


