>'milo' to it.  Under ARC, I tried to add a boot menu item (the same way
>I did the floppy one), but ARC wouldn't recognise the file system on
>sda1.  
>
>I did NOT dos format the partition sda1, just copied the files from the
>floppy disk using mcopy.  Since I don't have NT installed, I don't know
>how to format a partition into dos format.  
>
>Any help appreciated.
>
>Weiping

Probably the easiest way is to run arcinst.exe from the ARC menu entry for
"Run a program".

Arcinst.exe can be obtained at:
http://www.windowsnt.digital.com/support/drivers/drivers.asp

The built-in tools in most versions of ARC can't properly handle disks with
capacities over 2GB.
ARCINST.EXE doesn't have this problem. It works for all versions of Alpha
running on ARC firmware.


