Following up on myself:
 
> 	Apparently the problem is centered on the  gcc-2.7.2.3 vs.
> 	egcs-1.0.3a (which is known as egcs-1.0.2-8 on RH5.1; I know,
> 	I just made a diff against the sources.)

Well, no.  There is following type code:

Bool function (params)
{
	...
	if (funcpointer != NULL)
		return (funcpointer)(...)
}

That global "funcpointer" is always NULL in the XFree86, and
result of this code fragment depends on how used compiler happens
to scatter registers.

With gcc 2.7.2* this returns non-zero ("true"), and with egcs
it returns zero ("false")..


For sake of curiousity I am now doing
	make World CC="egcs -g -Wall"
