Hi,

From: Richard Henderson <rth@dot.cygnus.com>
Subject: Re: On Alpha, SQRT slows down after RH5.1 upgrade

rth> > 	mult/su	$f11, $f13, $f10	# fm    : $f10 = (x * 0.5) * y
rth> > 	mult	$f10, $f13, $f10	# fm    : $f10 = ((x * 0.5) * y) * y
rth> > 	subt	$f15, $f10, $f1		# fa    : $f1 = (1.5 - 0.5*x*y*y)
rth> > 	mult	$f13, $f1, $f13         # fm    : yp = y*(1.5 - 0.5*x*y*y)
rth> >  	mult/su	$f11, $f13, $f1		# fm    : $f11 = x * 0.5 * yp
rth> > 	mult	$f1,  $f13, $f11	# fm    : $f11 = (x * 0.5 * yp) * yp
rth> 
rth> You need to care for the trap shadow, don't you?  Or do we
rth> get away with this because the result is used the next insn?

Usually, we must add "trapb" after floating point insn.  But in
this case, we do not have to,  because of the dependency of $f10.

Rather, it's more important how to use registers. According to
original source,

  	mult	$f11, $f13, $f11	# fm    : $f11 = x * 0.5 * yp
 	mult	$f11, $f13, $f11	# fm    : $f11 = (x * 0.5 * yp) * yp

This first "mult" occurs SIG_FPE.  We can modify to

  	mult/su	$f11, $f13, $f11	# fm    : $f11 = x * 0.5 * yp
	trapb
 	mult	$f11, $f13, $f11	# fm    : $f11 = (x * 0.5 * yp) * yp

But we can not correct value($f11), because when we get SIG_FPE,
$f11 had alreadly been overwirtten with another value.  So, the
kernel can not set the correct value.

I'm sorry that yesterday's patch is not enough to avoid SIG_FPE in the 
much smaller value(i.e. 2.3e-308).  At first, I thouth we had to add
"trapb" after "subt/su",  but it seems unnecessary as long as I checked.

Thanks,
  goto@statabo.rim.or.jp


--- w_sqrt.S.old	Fri Jun 26 21:34:47 1998
+++ w_sqrt.S	Fri Jun 26 21:38:39 1998
@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@
 	mult	$f13, $f1, $f13		# fm    : ypp = $f13 = yp*$f1
 	subt	$f15, $f12, $f1		# fa    : $f1 = (1.5 - 0.5)
 	ldt	$f15, UP(t3)		# .. e1 :
-	mult	$f16, $f13, $f10	# fm    : z = $f10 = x * ypp
+	mult/su	$f16, $f13, $f10	# fm    : z = $f10 = x * ypp
 	mult	$f10, $f13, $f11	# fm    : $f11 = z*ypp
 	mult	$f10, $f12, $f12	# fm    : $f12 = z*0.5
 	subt	$f1, $f11, $f1		# .. fa : $f1 = 1 - z*ypp
@@ -137,11 +137,11 @@
 	mult/c	$f0, $f12, $f1		# fm    : $f1 = zp * zmi
 	mult/c	$f0, $f11, $f15		# fm    : $f15 = zp * zpl
 
-	subt    $f1, $f16, $f13		# fa    : y1 = zp*zmi - x
-	subt    $f15, $f16, $f15	# fa    : y2 = zp*zpl - x
+	subt/su $f1, $f16, $f13		# fa    : y1 = zp*zmi - x
+	subt/su $f15, $f16, $f14	# fa    : y2 = zp*zpl - x
 
 	fcmovge	$f13, $f12, $f0		# res = (y1 >= 0) ? zmi : res
-	fcmovlt	$f15, $f11, $f0		# res = (y2 <  0) ? zpl : res
+	fcmovlt	$f14, $f11, $f0		# res = (y2 <  0) ? zpl : res
 
 	ret
 


