On Fri, Jun 26, 1998 at 01:34:29PM +0800, Mikolaj J. Habryn wrote:

>   Does anyone have a PW500a running a 2.1 kernel (preferably 2.1.107
> or something relatively recent)? I am having remarkably little luck in
> convincing my box to work, and would deeply appreciate a known working
> .config along with versions for binutils, gcc/egcs, firmware and
> milo. Many thanks.

I've got debian hamm installed on my Miata (433a), and pristine 2.1.107
with SMP=1 commented out works fine for me.

There are some problems with it, which also happen on intel, though: 

* fbcon is totally broken (doesn't even compile on alpha)
* shift-pageup doesn't work
* some "spelling corrections" break some /proc-based packages

MILO is the latest Miata MILO from
gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels (yes, Kernels, *NOT*
Miniloaders!), the firmware is AlphaBios 5.25. 

The rest is from latest debian hamm (as stated above), i.e. egcs 1.0.3 and
binutils 2.9.1

My .config is attached... copy it into /usr/src/linux and make oldconfig,
then answer any questions which may pop up (I'm always asked about using
SRM as a bootloader, which I don't want to) and you should be set. If you
have an Adaptec 2940, that is :)

I can also send you my vmlinux.gz if you suspect your compiler's at
fault...

Feel free to ask me if you still got problems.

-- 
Andreas Trottmann <andreas.trottmann@werft22.com>

--oyUTqETQ0mS9luUI
