Hello Dave,

I thought about the patches you are suggesting:

+++ ./include/Xpoll.h	Sat Jun 27 23:47:02 1998
+++ ./programs/Xserver/dix/Makefile	Sun Jun 28 00:22:35 1998
+++ ./programs/Xserver/dix/ffsl.c	Sun Jun 28 01:18:37 1998
+++ ./programs/Xserver/include/dix.h	Sun Jun 28 00:27:39 1998
+++ ./programs/Xserver/os/connection.c	Sun Jun 28 01:35:28 1998
+++ ./programs/Xserver/os/WaitFor.c	Sun Jun 28 01:35:16 1998
+++ ./programs/Xserver/Makefile	Sun Jun 28 01:04:13 1998

The first problem I see is that you are patching   Makefile:s
Those are GENERATED from  Imakefile:s  in the same directories.

The second is what I think larger system problem, as apparently
the codes in  connection.c,  and WaitFor.c assume select(2)
semantics with components of the fd_set's array to have size of
32 bits (and hence that ffs() works always, and that magic "i << 5"
type code is always correct..)

These same problems are in Opengroup X11R6.4 sources too.  Sigh..
(And in XFree86 betas too, for that matter)

/Matti Aarnio <matti.aarnio@sonera.fi>


