On 22 Jun, Francois LAPERRUQUE wrote:
> Hello everybody,
> I'm new to this mailling list but I hope someone will be able to help me ;-)
> I've just upgraded my 21164PC based alpha station from 64Mb to 256Mb of RAM
> because I need a "lot of RAM" for my fortran 90 programs (NAG compiler and
> libraries).
> The bad news are that I've never been able to boot correctly, I see a kernel
> panic at boot time (for example when checking HD) and if sometimes I get the
> login prompt, as soon as I log in, the system is crashing with a kernel
> panic.
> Before trying to change my new RAM, I would like to know if there are known
> problems with this kind of configuration.

If you are booting from ARC or AlphaBIOS, try upgrading to the latest
version of linload.exe and milo.  There was an old problem with linload
where it used a char (i.e. ONE BYTE) to pass the system memory size 
(in megabytes) to MILO.  Needless to say, things worked fine until
people started configuring systems with 256Mb or more.

Your problems may simply stem from the kernel being confused about
system memory size...

If the problem persists, let us know...

