On 29 Mar, Leslie Donaldson wrote:
>   I was trying to run wine under em86 . <grin>
>   I linked wine with the static option to avoid
> problems with gcc lib2.0 and now I get the following.
> 
> [root@shadowdragon src]# wine
> Unimplemented system call: modify_ldt(0x1, 0x7cfffc64, 0x10, 0x7cfffc9c,
> 0x0, 0x7cfffc74)

Don't bother even trying...

The x86 emulator inside of em86 can only emulate *user-mode* code in a
flat address space.  It doesn't know anything about x86 protected-mode
stuff (e.g. descriptor tables, segments, etc.).  To add this stuff would
slow down the emulator several-fold.

Bottom line: you won't get wine working under em86.  sorry 8-)

